WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.190
Cochabamba, Bolivia.

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:08.710
From 1 November 1999, a consortium
part-owned by the US company Bechtel runs the

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.890
city's water and sewer system.

4
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.210
In January 2000, water rates rise.

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.430
By an average of 35
per cent, Bechtel says.

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.710
By more than 50 per
cent, says Earthjustice.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.390
In April 2000, after mass protests,
the government rescinds the contract.

8
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.830
When does local resistance
to global forces succeed?

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.570
Never?

10
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.410
Only when courts decide?

11
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.070
Only in rich countries?

12
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.470
In this mission, you'll follow
resistance at every scale,

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.510
from Cochabamba's water to Slow
Food, born in Rome in 1986.

14
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.790
Then you'll analyse three Swiss
votes on limiting immigration,

15
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.970
from 2014 to 2026.

16
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.840
Your mission: explain when local
resistance to global forces succeeds.
